# Day 6: Common attack types

## What I learned
- Brute force: many failed logins (T1110)
- Phishing: fake email or site to steal data (T1566)
- Malware: harmful program, may show as an unknown process (4688)
- Lateral movement: attacker moves between computers (T1021)

## My answer to the test question
- 10 succesful logins to different computers at 3 AM = lateral movement
- L1 checks account type, time, logon type and source IP, then escalates to L2 with evidence

